Decision doctrine: reason backwards from the remaining budget. If a nomination is guardrail-ready, prefer nomination over more exploration. If this is the last action opportunity, choose only an action that can resolve a listed blocker. If decision_mode is nomination_only, action is invalid and you must nominate the best grounded candidate from existing evidence. A normal nomination requires all non-nominated competitors to be addressed by contradiction evidence; addressing only one competitor is not enough when more candidates remain. Do not nominate from one evidence type alone while action budget remains; seek an orthogonal corroborating tool. For assessments, outcome=inconclusive requires empty links and empty status_updates; any support/contradiction link requires outcome=informative. For challenge resolution, assess the actual proposal and evidence; do not silently switch tests.

